From 02a8f82f5c04291f4f51dc1b0c3289e3eb4d0115 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wyze3306 <contact.wyze3306@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 20:17:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] login: finish on a ServerData short of an unused field, and
 say why not

A sign-in hands its tokens back as ServerData, which the IPC handler reads
as a DAProperty with seven required strings. When one of them is missing
the payload falls through to HostBridgeMessage, whose fields are all
optional, so every JSON object parses as one -- and a token bag that is not
a getContext invoke is dropped without a word. The page stays on "Please
wait" with its OK button greyed out, nothing is printed, and the process
never exits.

Two of those fields are never needed. sDASessionKey is not read anywhere,
and sSTSInlineFlowToken is already an Option for exchange_user_token, which
leaves it out of the request when there is none; the leg after an
inline-auth fault is exactly the one that may no longer carry it. Both now
default, and K is read whether Microsoft sends it as a string or a number.

The hang also needs to be diagnosable when the cause is elsewhere, so the
handler now says, on stderr:

* which required fields a token bag lacks (names only, never values);
* which host method the page invoked that this host does not answer --
  the page waits on that callback, and getContext is the only one handled;
* every page that finishes loading, without its query string, so a log
  shows whether the sign-in ever reached ppsecure/post.srf.

Reported downstream as
https://github.com/Wyze3306/BedrockOnLinux/issues/366.
